**AGRICULTURAL PRODUCTION AND SUPPLY AGREEMENT**

**This Agricultural Production and Supply Agreement (“Agreement”) is entered into as of this 1st day of February, 2023, by and between:**

**1. Green Valley Farms, LLC**  
   Address: 1234 Harvest Lane  
   Springfield, IL 62701  
   (Hereinafter referred to as "Producer")

**2. Prairie Grain Co., Inc.**  
   Address: 5678 Grain Exchange Blvd.  
   Chicago, IL 60603  
   (Hereinafter referred to as "Buyer")  

**RECITALS**

WHEREAS, Producer is engaged in the business of farming, including the cultivation of various crops and the rearing of livestock on their property located at 1234 Harvest Lane, Springfield, IL (the “Farm”);

WHEREAS, Buyer is engaged in the business of purchasing agricultural commodities and distributing them throughout the Midwest region, including but not limited to grain, corn, soybeans, and livestock products;

WHEREAS, Producer and Buyer desire to enter into this Agreement to set forth the terms and conditions under which the Producer will supply agricultural products to the Buyer.

**NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual promises and covenants herein contained, the parties agree as follows:**

**1. DEFINITIONS**  
For the purposes of this Agreement, the following terms shall have the meanings set forth below:

1.1 “Crops” refers to all agricultural produce cultivated by the Producer, including but not limited to corn (Zea mays), soybeans (Glycine max), and wheat (Triticum aestivum).

1.2 “Livestock” refers to all farm animals raised by the Producer, including but not limited to cattle (Bos taurus), pigs (Sus scrofa), and poultry.

1.3 “Irrigation System” refers to the infrastructure installed on the Farm to facilitate the efficient watering of Crops, including but not limited to drip irrigation and center pivot irrigation systems.

1.4 “Commodities” refers to the products derived from the Crops and Livestock, including but not limited to grain, meat, dairy, and processed foods.

**2. SCOPE OF SUPPLY**  
2.1 The Producer agrees to supply to the Buyer the following commodities during the term of this Agreement:

   a. **Corn**: A minimum of 100,000 bushels per harvest season, delivered in accordance with the delivery schedule outlined in Exhibit A.

   b. **Soybeans**: A minimum of 50,000 bushels per harvest season, delivered in accordance with the delivery schedule outlined in Exhibit A.

   c. **Cattle**: A minimum of 200 head of cattle annually, to be delivered to Buyer's facility located at 7890 Meat Processing Rd., Chicago, IL.

   d. **Pork**: A minimum of 1,000 hogs annually, to be delivered in accordance with the delivery schedule outlined in Exhibit A.

2.2 All deliveries shall comply with the quality specifications set forth in Exhibit B.

**3. DELIVERY AND ACCEPTANCE**  
3.1 The Producer shall deliver the Crops and Livestock to the Buyer at the specified locations as set forth in Exhibit A. Each delivery shall be accompanied by a delivery note indicating the quantity and type of Commodities delivered.

